# Rollback Strategy

## A. Local merge problem

If conflict resolution is wrong:

```text
STOP
```

Do not reset the source branches.

Discard/recreate only the disposable integration branch if necessary.

Original contributor branches remain untouched.

---

## B. Preprod application problem

Redeploy the last known-good preprod SHA.

Keep the merge branch intact for investigation.

Do not rewrite history.

---

## C. Preprod DB problem

Use the documented migration rollback or restore procedure.

Do not casually delete/alter production-like data to "make tests pass."

---

## D. Netlify problem

Immediately redeploy the last known-good deployment/commit.

Then investigate the merge branch separately.

---

## E. Production application problem

If DB is compatible with the previous application version:

```text
rollback application → last known-good SHA
```

If DB has changed incompatibly:

```text
do NOT blindly roll back application
```

Instead determine whether:

1. forward-fix is safer, or
2. DB rollback/restore is required.

